cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HippoMCP: A Long-Term Memory Layer for LLM Hosts via MCP"
abstract: >-
  A service that provides long-term memory to LLM hosts through MCP
  (Model Context Protocol). Unlike "adding a vector store to an app",
  it covers the full path from writing, retrieval, and curation to
  hand-assembled context slots: a four-layer memory model (raw stream /
  facts / summaries / profile), cascade deletion with tombstones,
  a superseded state machine (old facts are marked superseded, not erased),
  CfC-based temporal encoding inspired by liquid neural networks,
  and 5-slot context assembly with an independent token budget.
authors:
